// Lesson 2 — Math: inline and display equations, named symbols, no backslashes.

= Method

Let $t_"setup"$ and $t_"write"$ be the hours spent tinkering and writing. We
define the _tinkering ratio_

$ r = t_"setup" / (t_"setup" + t_"write") $ <eq:ratio>

Assuming that only $t_"write"$ advances the dissertation, the time to submission
relative to a baseline $T_0$ grows without bound as $r arrow.r 1$:

$ T_"sub" = T_0 / (1 - r) $ <eq:divergence>
